  "overview": "**Wanda Design System** is a light-first design system anchored on `hsl(0 0% 100%)` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#e00000` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `token(--wds-font-family-sans)` (16px display down to 16px body), unified by `8px` base corner radius and stepped `hsl(0 0% 100%)` -> `hsl(220 20% 98%)` surface layering.\n\nMaintained by **Wonderflow**. Source: published token package (https://github.com/wonderflow-bv/wanda), repo https://github.com/wonderflow-bv/wanda. Inventory: **91** colors, **3** typography steps, and **8** documented components (see repository license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 8 component tokens with documented paddings: `8px 12px`, `2px`, `6px 12px`, `12px 14px`, `10px 14px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `hsl(220 20% 98%)` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Surface & Stroke Elevation**: Relies on crisp tonal contrast (`hsl(0 0% 100%)` -> `hsl(220 20% 98%)`) and `1px solid color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines instead of heavy drop shadows.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#e00000` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `hsl(0 0% 100%)` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#e00000` with `#f7f7f8` text (4.7:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `token(--wds-font-family-sans)` headings with `token(--wds-font-family-sans)` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `8px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (8px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `hsl(220 20% 98%)` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `8px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input` fields and secondary buttons."
}
